    UX-002 complete on c73c0d65 (merge of wt/UX-002): package.json now carries
    pretest=npm run build so `npm install && npm test` works on a clone that has no
    dist/, and every fixed setTimeout(1500) readiness gate in the arch002 daemon test
    is a bounded poll. Verified on an install-only clone (dist ABSENT after install,
    npm test exit 0, 1944 passed | 58 skipped, 0 failed), 3 consecutive arch002 runs
    green at loadavg ~114, and CI run on c73c0d65 = success on the 2-core runner
    that had failed the same test on fe1f949d.
    
    QA-SPECLANG-2 gets acceptance criteria plus the live CI-red evidence; it stays
    pending as the lineage record for the arch002 flake class rather than a duplicate
    dispatch of the work UX-002 just landed.
    
    QA-SPECLANG-009 filed from a measurement this tick did not chase: the suite
    rebuilds dist/ mid-run because the hello-world spec's step 2 is `npm run build`
    and its verification test executes the spec verbatim from the repo root. That is
    a confounder for every other flake investigation here (2 of 6 full runs collided
    in this tick's session: pack-contract EOF on dist/src/tools/file-tools.js, and a
    30s timeout in tests/db.test.ts while tsc ran).
    
    Judge note recorded on UX-002: the tier-2 run 992ed787 hit the 100-iteration cap
    with 0 of 1 criteria graded (overall FAIL for ungraded coverage), so the close
    rests on the foreman gates and the green CI run, not on a judge PASS.
    
